      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Posting here for anyone else who comes across this issue and gets stumped. I had coffee and looked at the issue from another angle, I learned that unlike sdk2 where gestures would always go back to a neutral pose this isent the case in sdk3, if any of your gesture animations effect dynamic bone gravity then all of your other animations need to have the default values so the ear gravity isent always on what the animation is. The real answer is to create an animation with the default values of the ears put it on its own layer in the controller it dosent pop back to its normal state like sdk2 automatically you need to actually tell it to do that.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
